.bridgie/specs/statement-review/design.md:347:- **Log lines:** one structured line per event in the case log, with the event, case id, snapshot and counts, and no names or descriptions. For example: event=pack_written traced=100 reconciled=true unexplained_pct=12.4 cash_flagged=3 policy_check=shown.
.bridgie/specs/statement-review/design.md:348:- **What fires when it does not work:** there is no remote alerting, by design. Instead the tool refuses, with a non-zero exit and a red banner, when reconciliation fails, the guard fails, the log chain breaks, or a hosted model is requested under the offline lock. `cma report` exits non-zero if any case has traced figures below 100% or reconciled false.
